WEBVTT

01:53.226 --> 01:55.732
Vearn: But I shall
grant you that chance.

01:55.765 --> 01:59.138
These two will not intervene.

01:59.172 --> 02:02.812
You have an opportunity
to defeat me at last.

02:02.846 --> 02:05.183
That is your reward.

02:05.751 --> 02:07.121
Shall we, then?

02:07.154 --> 02:09.358
Surely you won't refuse me?

02:09.392 --> 02:11.029
Well, of course not.

02:11.062 --> 02:13.466
Even if you had
Mystvearn and the Reaper-

02:13.501 --> 02:15.070
we're not gonna back down.

02:15.103 --> 02:16.238
We've come this far and

02:16.272 --> 02:18.745
won every battle
along the way.

02:18.778 --> 02:20.548
Vearn: Very well.

02:21.249 --> 02:23.353
Then let us begin.

02:28.597 --> 02:31.235
I almost forgot.

02:31.268 --> 02:33.507
Vearn: That man.

02:33.541 --> 02:37.047
His ability to fight
was magnificent.

02:37.080 --> 02:41.156
He truly lived up to
the legends, but sadly,

02:41.189 --> 02:44.896
it seems his heart
was far too human.

02:44.930 --> 02:47.100
At least let me
give him an end

02:47.134 --> 02:50.273
befitting such an
impressive creature.

03:03.801 --> 03:05.839
Everyone, run!

03:05.872 --> 03:07.809
Popp: It's a Kafrizz spell!

03:08.877 --> 03:10.313
Oh, no - Dad!

03:10.346 --> 03:11.951
[shocked gasps]

03:11.984 --> 03:15.691
Vearn: [chuckling]

03:15.724 --> 03:16.927
Disappointed?

03:16.961 --> 03:21.435
Or perhaps you had wished
to send him off yourself, boy?

03:21.804 --> 03:23.273
[roaring]

03:23.307 --> 03:25.210
W-Wait. Dai, don't!

03:26.981 --> 03:27.949
[gasps]

03:36.633 --> 03:37.836
Oh, my.

03:37.869 --> 03:42.111
It seems your precious little
Hero was the first to fall.

03:42.144 --> 03:43.748
And I don't believe any of you

03:43.781 --> 03:47.655
have the power
necessary to harm me.

03:49.392 --> 03:52.264
Crocodine [thought]: He took
down Dai with one blow?!

03:52.297 --> 03:55.137
Hyunckel [thought]:
I've never seen such power.

03:55.170 --> 03:57.508
Vearn: What a disappointment.

03:57.542 --> 04:00.313
I even gave him a chance.

04:00.347 --> 04:04.689
Instead you would
follow your father, Hero?

04:05.424 --> 04:07.862
You guys - we need to move!

04:09.732 --> 04:10.267
[charing yell]

04:10.300 --> 04:12.003
I don't think so!

04:12.271 --> 04:14.843
Kafrizz!

04:20.922 --> 04:21.924
Now, Maam!

04:21.957 --> 04:24.228
I won't be able to
hold him off for very long.

04:24.261 --> 04:25.564
You have to heal Dai!

04:25.598 --> 04:26.600
I'll try!

04:30.641 --> 04:31.776
[alarmed breath]

04:33.246 --> 04:35.518
[screaming]

04:35.551 --> 04:36.754
Popp!

04:36.787 --> 04:37.555
Both: Popp!

04:41.730 --> 04:42.698
Hyunckel: No...

04:45.203 --> 04:46.940
Okay... That hurt.

04:46.974 --> 04:50.514
Did he really just burn
through enchanted clothing?

04:51.248 --> 04:52.151
[struggling grunt]

04:52.184 --> 04:54.723
And with such a tiny ember...

04:54.756 --> 04:56.826
How's it possible
that his Kafrizz spell

04:56.860 --> 04:59.198
is so much stronger
than my own?!

04:59.232 --> 05:01.770
Kafrizz? Don't be absurd.

05:01.803 --> 05:05.377
It was a much simpler
spell than that.

05:05.410 --> 05:07.515
It's "Frizz."

05:08.183 --> 05:09.385
A Frizz?!

05:09.419 --> 05:11.690
I suppose no one told you.

05:11.723 --> 05:14.295
The effect of a spell
can vary greatly

05:14.328 --> 05:17.969
depending on the caster's
overall Magic Power.

05:18.002 --> 05:22.311
Even though they're both
fire-type spells, in essence...

05:22.344 --> 05:23.614
Any magic of mine

05:23.647 --> 05:26.720
will be unfathomably
greater than yours.

05:27.187 --> 05:28.223
W-What?!

05:28.256 --> 05:30.461
Vearn: Such a
difference in strength.

05:30.494 --> 05:31.830
You've managed to overwhelm

05:31.863 --> 05:35.437
the Dark Army's forces
time and time again,

05:35.470 --> 05:38.644
so I assumed you would be
a little more powerful,

05:38.678 --> 05:40.881
but it seems I was wrong.

05:40.915 --> 05:44.556
Even the boy, Dai,
all I had to do was

05:44.590 --> 05:49.098
use a small fraction of
my Aura to match his attack.

05:49.132 --> 05:51.068
Let me demonstrate.

06:03.026 --> 06:05.632
Hyunckel: Super-pressurized
Dark Aura...

06:05.665 --> 06:07.535
That's what he used on Dai?!

06:07.568 --> 06:10.975
Right - if we really
want to win this battle,

06:11.009 --> 06:12.813
then we must fight as one!

06:12.846 --> 06:15.484
Maam, do you think
he's gonna be all right?

06:15.518 --> 06:17.454
His heart's beating, but...

06:17.488 --> 06:20.761
His body can only
take so much damage.

06:20.795 --> 06:24.434
Maam: He was hit precisely where
he'd already been wounded.

06:25.203 --> 06:28.476
Please... Just heal
him already!

06:28.510 --> 06:30.180
I'm trying, but it won't work.

06:30.213 --> 06:31.750
It's no use.

06:32.719 --> 06:35.423
As much as I enjoy
watching you weaklings

06:35.456 --> 06:38.262
struggle to summon
your courage...

06:38.296 --> 06:40.568
you're only wasting time.

06:40.601 --> 06:43.641
It seems like all
along I've miscalculated

06:43.674 --> 06:47.381
the Hero and his party's
prowess in battle.

06:47.414 --> 06:50.454
Even if Dai were still
amongst your ranks,

06:50.487 --> 06:52.892
it would change nothing.

06:52.925 --> 06:55.898
And so, as recompense
for my error,

06:55.931 --> 06:59.739
allow me to destroy
all of you, painlessly.

07:15.237 --> 07:17.742
This is my Kafrizz spell.

07:17.775 --> 07:19.444
With its unimaginable power

07:19.478 --> 07:22.250
and the graceful
form it takes on...

07:22.284 --> 07:25.557
it has its own name
in the Underworld.

07:26.559 --> 07:29.197
Kaiser Phoenix.

07:35.143 --> 07:36.145
Hyunckel!

07:37.548 --> 07:39.318
Hyunckel: My armor
should be able to

07:39.351 --> 07:40.921
withstand it for a moment...

07:40.955 --> 07:42.692
Hurry and heal Dai!

07:46.498 --> 07:47.467
Another one?!

07:47.502 --> 07:49.539
But, how?! He's too fast!

07:58.089 --> 08:07.308
[pained screaming]

08:07.341 --> 08:10.013
I can't heal him like this!

08:10.046 --> 08:13.653
Everyone; we're going
on the offensive!

08:25.277 --> 08:28.750
Dark King... It's time!

08:38.604 --> 08:41.543
Hyunckel: Bloody... Scryde!

08:43.246 --> 08:44.014
Hyunckel: [surprised breath]

08:44.047 --> 08:45.951
Such optimism.

08:45.985 --> 08:47.220
Revolting.

08:47.253 --> 08:51.228
The darkness you kept
was far more magnificent.

08:51.930 --> 08:53.099
[roaring]

08:53.132 --> 08:55.103
[battle cry]

08:58.544 --> 09:00.313
Curse you!

09:01.381 --> 09:04.054
[pained scream]

09:08.597 --> 09:10.199
Crocodine!

09:11.937 --> 09:13.272
Look out!

09:17.982 --> 09:19.317
No - Hyunckel!

09:20.320 --> 09:22.691
Popp: Hey - over here!

09:26.265 --> 09:27.668
My, my...

09:29.471 --> 09:30.574
Popp [thought]: Here goes...

09:30.607 --> 09:32.077
If I can't beat him with this,

09:32.111 --> 09:34.782
then I'll be completely
out of spells to try.

09:34.816 --> 09:37.187
So, please... work!

09:37.822 --> 09:39.592
Medroa!

09:42.363 --> 09:43.534
What?! No way...

09:43.567 --> 09:45.336
This is Bounce.

09:51.014 --> 09:53.152
Popp [thought]: I'll
have to cancel it out.

09:58.597 --> 09:59.665
Popp!

10:08.918 --> 10:11.122
Maam: Popp, are you okay?!

10:11.155 --> 10:12.123
Wh-what now?

10:12.157 --> 10:14.662
He managed to deflect
it with a Bounce spell.

10:14.696 --> 10:17.200
Even Medroa doesn't
seem to work.

10:17.233 --> 10:21.075
How did he conjure that
spell so quickly, anyway?!

10:21.108 --> 10:23.647
Hyunckel: He's on
a different level.

10:23.681 --> 10:24.582
Popp: Huh?

10:24.616 --> 10:26.753
His power seems
to be limitless.

10:26.787 --> 10:28.791
It's almost like
he can cast a spell

10:28.824 --> 10:32.230
without even needing
the time to charge it up.

10:32.264 --> 10:37.641
That lets him do two things in
the time it takes us to do one.

10:37.675 --> 10:39.178
So, while we're attacking,

10:39.211 --> 10:43.419
he can defend as he
conjures a counterstrike.

10:52.103 --> 10:54.909
Hey, Maam. Can you
take Dai, too?

10:54.943 --> 10:55.611
Huh?

10:55.644 --> 10:56.914
Get them to Crocodine.

10:56.947 --> 10:58.750
Then we'll Zoom outta here.

10:58.784 --> 11:00.788
It's the only
option we have left.

11:00.821 --> 11:02.190
Are you sure?

11:02.224 --> 11:05.731
Popp: There's nothing we can
do against a force like him.

11:05.764 --> 11:08.504
No wonder he's called
the God of the Underworld.

11:08.537 --> 11:10.641
We're being toyed with-

11:10.674 --> 11:12.410
like he's holding
back or something.

11:12.443 --> 11:13.981
If we really want
to fight him,

11:14.014 --> 11:15.584
we'll need to regroup first...

11:15.617 --> 11:17.353
or we're done for.

11:20.594 --> 11:21.963
Okay, then.

11:22.565 --> 11:24.702
C'mon. Here goes.

11:24.735 --> 11:26.171
Bye, old man!

11:29.779 --> 11:31.281
Popp: Zoom!

11:33.352 --> 11:34.822
Popp: What?! No!

11:34.855 --> 11:39.832
[pained groans]

11:43.740 --> 11:45.210
What was that?!

11:45.243 --> 11:46.412
Killvearn: Poor things.

11:46.445 --> 11:50.119
They're just the picture
of hopelessness, aren't they?

11:50.654 --> 11:53.159
Do you understand, now?

11:53.193 --> 11:56.799
There's no one who
can escape the Dark King.

12:09.358 --> 12:11.162
Killvearn: [chuckling]

12:11.195 --> 12:15.103
The palace is shielded by
King Vearn's Magic Power.

12:15.136 --> 12:18.743
You won't be able to
escape it with a Zoom spell.

12:20.246 --> 12:23.787
Killvearn: Sure, you can
move within the force field.

12:23.821 --> 12:25.423
But while the
shield is active

12:25.456 --> 12:28.864
no one may enter... or leave.

12:28.897 --> 12:30.066
No one, that is,

12:30.100 --> 12:34.976
except for certain
warriors of the Dark Army.

12:35.009 --> 12:37.515
Killvearn: If you'd tried
to fight instead of running,

12:37.548 --> 12:40.821
you might have lasted
just a little bit longer.

12:40.854 --> 12:42.024
[amused chuckle]

12:42.057 --> 12:44.295
But I guess
it's all the same.

12:44.328 --> 12:47.669
Either way, there's
nothing you can do.

12:47.702 --> 12:49.238
Piroro: You're all done for!

12:49.271 --> 12:50.841
You're all toast!

12:50.875 --> 12:52.645
[disagreeing chirps]

12:52.679 --> 12:54.314
What's your problem?

12:54.347 --> 12:57.387
I said that you're all
toast, toast, toast!

12:57.421 --> 12:58.857
[disagreeing chirps]

12:58.891 --> 13:01.061
Piroro:
You're! All! Done! For!

13:01.095 --> 13:02.296
Gomechan: [defiant chirps]

13:03.399 --> 13:04.769
They're quite right.

13:04.803 --> 13:06.973
Now, to finish the battle.

13:12.852 --> 13:15.289
I must have made contact...

13:15.824 --> 13:17.461
A minute ago...

13:17.494 --> 13:19.265
with my Refractor Fist!

13:19.298 --> 13:20.200
Right!

13:20.233 --> 13:22.370
Back when everyone
attacked all at once!

13:27.080 --> 13:30.353
Killvearn: You landed
a hit. What a shock.

13:30.387 --> 13:31.823
Maam [thought]: It worked!

13:31.857 --> 13:35.230
That means the Dark King
is still a living creature.

13:35.263 --> 13:38.435
If I can hit him with
my Refractor Fist...

13:39.539 --> 13:42.277
Well, care to try?

13:42.311 --> 13:46.385
It's a one-in-a-million
chance of success, girl.

13:46.418 --> 13:51.596
My servants won't intervene and
if I happen to be wounded...

13:51.629 --> 13:55.036
My attacks will become slower.

13:55.069 --> 14:00.112
But, surely you know that
Darklings can regenerate.

14:02.116 --> 14:06.793
If you don't hurry,
you might lose your chance.

14:06.827 --> 14:08.830
Maam [thought]:
We can't escape,

14:08.863 --> 14:11.435
and I'm the only one
left who can fight...

14:11.468 --> 14:13.973
Vearn: What will you do?

14:14.007 --> 14:15.544
Maam [thought]:
I have to try!

14:16.680 --> 14:17.881
Don't!

14:27.367 --> 14:28.469
Slow down.

14:28.503 --> 14:31.374
We're not going to win
this thing by going in alone.

14:32.077 --> 14:33.513
Killvearn: Very sharp.

14:33.546 --> 14:37.621
The little Mage may
even be halfway useful.

14:37.655 --> 14:38.857
You were toying with me...

14:38.890 --> 14:41.930
You could regenerate any time!

14:41.963 --> 14:43.634
You are so cruel.

14:43.667 --> 14:47.407
Maam: You enjoy playing
with us like that, don't you?

14:47.440 --> 14:49.846
Of course I do.

14:49.879 --> 14:52.016
To obtain such
immeasurable power

14:52.050 --> 14:55.725
and be able to use it
however you wish in life...

14:55.758 --> 14:58.129
Is that not pleasurable?

14:58.162 --> 15:00.968
Would you not feel superior?

15:01.001 --> 15:02.471
What do you mean?

15:02.505 --> 15:03.941
Power is the purest and

15:03.974 --> 15:07.147
most beautiful law of
the natural world.

15:07.180 --> 15:10.721
"Survival of the fittest"
is how all creatures live.

15:10.755 --> 15:13.393
From Darklings to Dragons.

15:13.426 --> 15:17.000
Only you humans use
your so called "reason"...

15:17.033 --> 15:19.204
to deny the truth.

15:19.238 --> 15:23.146
But power is the only thing
that matters in the end.

15:23.179 --> 15:25.116
But how can you decide that?

15:25.150 --> 15:28.121
Before you, monsters and
humans lived in peace.

15:28.155 --> 15:32.129
The Surface World isn't bound
by the same laws as yours!

15:33.566 --> 15:34.334
[startled breath]

15:34.367 --> 15:36.974
You are still
missing the point.

15:37.007 --> 15:39.444
The truth is that
peace can only ever be

15:39.477 --> 15:43.753
maintained by the
enforcement of a great power.

15:43.787 --> 15:45.156
A power...

15:45.190 --> 15:48.696
Wielded only by the gods!

15:51.101 --> 15:53.539
Vearn: My home,
the Underworld,

15:53.573 --> 15:58.651
is a realm that exists deep
in the earth below your own.

15:58.684 --> 16:00.220
Everywhere you look...

16:00.253 --> 16:04.562
nothing but barren
rock and boiling magma.

16:04.595 --> 16:06.432
What's more, the sun,

16:06.465 --> 16:10.507
the source of all life,
cannot shine below.

16:10.541 --> 16:11.776
The sun...

16:11.810 --> 16:13.914
Such a magnificent power.

16:13.947 --> 16:16.185
But the gods granted the sun

16:16.218 --> 16:19.525
and the Surface World
to the humans,

16:19.559 --> 16:23.132
banishing Darklings and
Dragons to the Underworld...

16:23.165 --> 16:27.206
simply because the humans
were that much weaker.

16:29.979 --> 16:31.314
Vearn: If that was justice,

16:31.348 --> 16:34.589
then our power
is justice, as well.

16:34.622 --> 16:36.258
So I waited.

16:36.292 --> 16:38.763
Thousands of years
passed in that time.

16:38.797 --> 16:43.305
All while I honed my skills to
someday annihilate your world.

16:43.339 --> 16:46.779
Soon, it will be no more.

16:46.813 --> 16:49.885
And the sun will
finally shine...

16:49.918 --> 16:53.560
I will bring it
to the Underworld.

16:53.594 --> 16:54.929
When that happens...

16:54.963 --> 16:57.200
I...

16:57.233 --> 17:01.041
I shall become the
true god of the realm.

17:01.074 --> 17:05.182
And then, the great
folly of the old gods...

17:05.216 --> 17:08.088
will be corrected at last.

17:12.396 --> 17:15.203
Popp [thought]:
W-We can't win...

17:15.236 --> 17:18.375
He's thinking on a
whole different scale.

17:18.409 --> 17:21.214
For thousands of years,
he's seen the Surface World

17:21.248 --> 17:24.522
as nothing but a
weight over his own.

17:24.555 --> 17:25.725
We're just...

17:25.758 --> 17:27.861
We're just mere humans.

17:27.895 --> 17:30.667
We don't have a
hope of beating him.

17:31.736 --> 17:34.108
You've finally given up.

17:34.141 --> 17:37.247
This was more
enjoyable than I expected.

17:37.280 --> 17:41.021
You've done so well,
Heroes of the Surface.

17:41.054 --> 17:43.258
I'm not giving up yet.

17:44.460 --> 17:46.131
Both: D-Dai?!

17:46.165 --> 17:48.737
Dai: Even if everyone
else in the world has,

17:48.770 --> 17:50.807
I still won't give up.

17:52.177 --> 17:54.080
Dai: I'll never give up!

17:54.114 --> 17:56.318
What impressive vitality.

17:56.352 --> 17:59.258
Could you repeat
that, young man?

17:59.291 --> 18:02.096
I'm sure I misheard you.

18:02.130 --> 18:04.835
I said I'm not giving up.

18:04.869 --> 18:07.808
Even if there's
really no hope left.

18:07.841 --> 18:09.177
I'm going to keep on fighting

18:09.210 --> 18:11.716
because it's what
I was meant to do.

18:11.749 --> 18:16.224
So, it seems I heard you
correctly the first time.

18:16.258 --> 18:18.596
Even after coming face
to face with my power,

18:18.630 --> 18:21.703
you still won't
back down from this.

18:21.736 --> 18:26.077
Dai: I know exactly how
overwhelming your power can be.

18:26.111 --> 18:28.448
But that doesn't
matter anymore.

18:30.285 --> 18:34.762
Dai: You said that power is
justice, but you're wrong.

18:35.698 --> 18:37.400
It's not.

18:37.434 --> 18:39.872
That's not what
Grampa taught me...

18:39.905 --> 18:41.543
Or what Master Avan
taught me...

18:41.576 --> 18:45.015
Or what Dad taught me
about justice...

18:45.049 --> 18:48.221
You're wrong about
every single thing!

18:51.563 --> 18:52.664
All: Dai!

18:59.979 --> 19:01.248
Mytsvearn [thought]:
They stand...

19:01.282 --> 19:04.454
After they were on
the verge of death?!

19:05.691 --> 19:07.327
As you wish.

19:07.360 --> 19:09.397
Such a persuasive soul,

19:09.430 --> 19:11.034
one that gives
your weak friends

19:11.068 --> 19:14.207
the strength to
somehow defy me.

19:14.241 --> 19:17.413
But your soul will lead
them to their demise.

19:17.446 --> 19:19.852
If you wish to change my mind,

19:19.885 --> 19:23.894
you'll have to reveal just
how powerful you really are.

19:23.927 --> 19:25.630
Then here we go...

19:27.066 --> 19:29.839
This is all of my power!

19:29.872 --> 19:32.778
Vearn: Kaiser Phoenix!

19:32.811 --> 19:37.854
Avan Strash!

19:39.525 --> 19:41.394
C'mon! Work!

19:42.030 --> 19:43.633
Too slow.

19:46.472 --> 19:47.741
Dai!

20:02.972 --> 20:04.340
Mystvearn: King Vearn!

20:04.374 --> 20:07.748
Vearn [thought]: He was able
to counter my second attack.

20:07.781 --> 20:09.250
And not only that,

20:09.284 --> 20:13.425
but his force overpowered
my Kaiser Phoenix.

20:14.294 --> 20:15.964
Very well!

20:18.368 --> 20:19.671
Boom spells?!

20:40.580 --> 20:45.624
Whoa! It's... like
a storm of Boom spells!

20:45.657 --> 20:48.630
Vearn's using weaker spells
and fighting with numbers!

20:48.663 --> 20:52.704
Each one of these is as
destructive as a Kaboom spell.

20:54.909 --> 20:55.910
No, Dai!

21:01.722 --> 21:04.762
Mystvearn: King Vearn,
perhaps it's time to put an end

21:04.796 --> 21:08.603
to these games and let
us all join the battle.

21:09.337 --> 21:13.212
Vearn: What? Ridiculous.

21:13.245 --> 21:15.884
You actually believe
the boy will survive

21:15.918 --> 21:17.921
this kind of attack?

21:20.259 --> 21:21.929
Dai, no!

21:23.098 --> 21:26.471
[roaring]

21:34.087 --> 21:35.322
Now...

21:35.356 --> 21:38.897
Take this!

21:38.930 --> 21:41.000
[overpowered roar]

21:42.236 --> 21:44.307
Mystvearn: King Vearn!

23:37.835 --> 23:40.339
Narrator: After surviving
Dai's Avan Strash,

23:40.373 --> 23:42.644
King Vearn summons
a legendary weapon,

23:42.678 --> 23:45.315
then delivers a
counterstrike powerful enough

23:45.349 --> 23:47.754
to shake the heavens
and the earth...

23:47.787 --> 23:50.492
And once he's driven
back his adversaries,

23:50.526 --> 23:53.566
the Dark King unleashes
his finishing blow.

23:53.600 --> 23:55.704
In the face of
almost certain doom,

23:55.737 --> 23:58.142
is there any hope
for Dai and his friends?

23:58.175 --> 23:59.512
Find out next time on

23:59.545 --> 24:01.950
Dragon Quest:
The Adventure of Dai,

24:01.983 --> 24:03.753
"The Unlikely Savior".
